blurb = "The poem in the yellow box on the top right is by Emperor Tenji (628 - 681). In the poem the Emperor takes shelter during an autumn rain in the field hut of a common rice farmer.

Coarse the rush-mat roof
Sheltering the harvest-hut
Of the autumn rice-field
And my sleeves are growing wet
With the moisture dripping through

Although the poet describes the rain dampening his sleeves, the image of wet sleeves was a common metaphor for weeping (the word tsuyu can mean dewdrops or tears)."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
